cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use source-to-skill in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: source-to-skill
version: 0.5.0
date-released: "2026-10-04"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Strnadel
    given-names: Michal
repository-code: "https://github.com/michalstrnadel/source-to-skill"
url: "https://github.com/michalstrnadel/source-to-skill"
abstract: >-
  source-to-skill turns YouTube videos, playlists and channels, podcasts and
  audio (transcribed locally with Whisper), arXiv and PDF papers, EPUB and PDF
  books, web articles, and GitHub repositories into agent skills. A
  deterministic, dependency-light extractor produces text plus structural
  segments without LLMs or API keys; the user's own coding agent then distills
  them into an installable skill following the Agent Skills standard, shipped
  as a Claude Code plugin.
keywords:
  - agent-skills
  - claude-code
  - llm
  - youtube
  - podcast
  - whisper
  - arxiv
  - pdf
  - epub
  - web-articles
  - github
  - knowledge-distillation
